argocd-server: The API/UI/CLI front end that handles authentication, RBAC, and webhooks, and doesn't reconcile anything itself.

argocd-repo-server: Clones Git repos and renders manifests (Helm, Kustomize, plain YAML) Responsible for turning source repositories into Kubernetes manifests.
Repo server generates desired manifests. It does not primarily decide whether the cluster is in sync.

argocd-application-controller: The reconciler that compares Git's desired state with live cluster state and syncs the differences.

argocd-applicationset-controller: Generates Application objects from templates and generators, for fleets of clusters or environments.
ApplicationSet
      |
      +---- dev     -> Application
      +---- staging -> Application
      +---- prod    -> Application
A common use case is deploying the same application to multiple clusters:

ApplicationSet (in the Argo CD cluster)
   │  cluster generator → one Application per registered cluster
   ├── App A (destination: cluster-a)  → deploys to cluster-a
   ├── App B (destination: cluster-b)  → deploys to cluster-b
   └── App C (destination: cluster-c)  → deploys to cluster-c


redis: A cache for manifests and app state that can be rebuilt from Git and the clusters if lost.

dex-server: An optional SSO broker that connects Argo CD login to identity providers like LDAP, SAML, or GitHub.

