Apps

the CLI talks to argocd-server, not directly to the application controller.

Similarly, when you open the Argo CD UI, your browser talks to argocd-server.

argocd app list
argocd app get <app>                 # status, health, resources
argocd app create <app> --repo <url> --path <dir> --dest-server https://kubernetes.default.svc --dest-namespace <ns>
argocd app sync <app>                # add --prune, --force, --dry-run
argocd app diff <app>                # live vs Git
argocd app history <app>
argocd app rollback <app> <id>
argocd app set <app> --sync-policy automated --self-heal --auto-prune
argocd app delete <app>              # add --cascade=false to keep resources
argocd app wait <app> --health
argocd app terminate-op <app>        # cancel a stuck sync
argocd app logs <app>

